mber 1999. Jack in the Box Inc. was founded in 1951 and is headquartered in San Diego, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Mark James King | Interim CEO & Executive Chairman | Age 65","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $1.1M ranks in the top quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $56K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $6K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Jack In The Box Inc. is a micro-cap consumer cyclical business with a $270M market cap on $1.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -0% over the past three years and -0% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 19% against a 7% cost of capital \u2014 a 12-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $74M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 5 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","Accruals are elevated at -9.4% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 41.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin -0.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 8.0% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 9.5% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 108% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.0788868480989238},{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (32.7% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Operating margins 9% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (80% sell ratio) over the past year","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.2},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 65/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; durably derated by the market \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Jack in the Box (NASDAQ:JACK) Stock Climbs Above Near-Term Average","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/consumer/jack-in-the-box-nasdaqjack-stock-climbs-above-near-term-average","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793720580.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.103,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"(JACK) Movement Within Algorithmic Entry Frameworks","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com